The demonstration account is a public on-chain example, **not the user's wallet**. Address and chain identify the tokens; symbols are display metadata. Full contract and controller addresses are in [the oracle investigation](docs/oracle-investigation.md).

## Reproducible single-position demo (synthetic fixtures)

```powershell
cd C:\liquidation-watchdog
npm ci
npm run build
npm run demo:submission
```

This runs one configured position through the real monitoring pipeline with deterministic local fixtures (never live chain data): warning then critical threshold states, non-financial actions while evidence is unverified, a separately labeled synthetic strict-gate scenario that is the only place a financial option can appear, SQLite alert/outbox persistence, console delivery, restart without resending known deliveries, and read-model output. Artifacts are written to `data/submission-demo/`. See [the demo guide](docs/SUBMISSION-SINGLE-POSITION-DEMO.md). All evidence remains `actionable: false`; oracle assurance stays `UNVERIFIED`/`UNKNOWN` outside the explicitly synthetic qualified scenario.

## Verification

```powershell
npm run verify
# After final documentation is complete against the tested inputs:
npm run verify -- --finalize
npm run release:manifest
npm run release:check
```

The full sequence has **26 checks**: strict typechecking, ESLint, the complete unit suite, a repeated operational subset, real RPC + MCP integration, deterministic bounded stability, build, live/historical CLI smokes, two one-cycle monitor processes, 15 operational CLI invocations, three bounded oracle audits and three persisted-status processes, source/runtime/evidence checks, exact Phase 2 replays, audit, secret scan, Phase 1–4 preservation, links, inventory and read-only Git whitespace checks. External notification tests use mocks only. Results and unique per-attempt transcripts are written under `evidence/phase5/`.

Finalization performs five local checks and rejects changes to tested source/configuration/scripts. The release manifest binds the tested inputs, build, documentation and evidence. New captures or later edits require re-verification/finalization and manifest regeneration as appropriate. Verification does not stage or commit files. See [Phase 5 results](docs/phase5-report.md#12-tests-and-exact-verification-results) and [testing](docs/testing.md).

